        "@@ -117,3 +117,3 @@\n",
        "     <h3>A further comparison in Unit 4</h3>",
        "-    <p>On the Unit 4 assessment, 25 of the 28 students produced explanations that met its criteria for phosphatase regulation and cancer-related cell growth. The question assessed a different mechanism, so the count cannot measure progress on a common scale. S06's two Unit 3 answers left the photosynthetic pathway undeveloped. Their Unit 4 explanation met that task's completeness criteria. S22 reconstructed the photosynthetic pathway completely in Unit 3, while their Unit 4 response left the connection between sustained signalling and growth restraint incomplete.</p>",
        "+    <p>In Unit 4, 25 of the 28 students gave explanations that met the criteria for that question, which concerned phosphatase regulation and cancer-related cell growth. As the task addressed a new mechanism, the count did not establish progress on a common measure. The individual records also resisted a simple progression narrative. S06 had left the photosynthetic pathway undeveloped in both Unit 3 answers, yet produced a complete Unit 4 explanation. S22 showed the reverse pattern, reconstructing the photosynthetic pathway completely while leaving the connection between sustained signalling and growth restraint incomplete in Unit 4. Completeness on one mechanism could not stand in for an assessment of the student's reasoning across contexts.</p>",
        "   </div>"
      ]
